---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
const updated = 'September 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — psiberAI"
  description="How psiberAI collects, uses, and protects personal data."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="faint" style="font-size:.86rem"><em>Last updated: {updated}. This is a starting policy to be reviewed and finalized with legal counsel before launch — bracketed items need completing.</em></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        psiberAI ("we", "us") provides security and AI-governance advisory services. For the purposes of
        data-protection law, the data controller is [legal entity name], [registered address].
        Questions about this policy or your data: <a href="mailto:privacy@psiberai.com">privacy@psiberai.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Information you send us</strong> — your name, email address, company and any details you include when you contact us or enquire about an assessment.</li>
        <li><strong>Basic analytics</strong> — aggregate, privacy-preserving usage statistics (page views, referrers) collected without cookies and without tracking you across sites.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not use advertising or cross-site tracking.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and deliver services you request.</li>
        <li>To send you material you have asked for (for example, the newsletter — only with your consent, and you can unsubscribe at any time).</li>
        <li>To understand, in aggregate, how the site is used so we can improve it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Lawful basis (UK/EU GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on your <strong>consent</strong> (for the newsletter), the <strong>performance of a contract</strong>
        or steps at your request (for enquiries and engagements), and our <strong>legitimate interests</strong>
        in operating and improving the site, balanced against your rights.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We share personal data only with service providers that help us operate — for example email and
        hosting providers — under appropriate agreements, and where required by law. Any client
        information handled during an engagement is governed by the confidentiality terms of that engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        We serve clients in the US, Europe, the UAE and Australia. Where personal data is transferred
        across borders, we use appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses) as required.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purpose it was collected, or as required by
        law, then delete or anonymize it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or port your data,
        to object to or restrict processing, and to withdraw consent. To exercise any of these, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@psiberai.com">privacy@psiberai.com</a>. You may also complain to your local
        data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses no advertising or tracking cookies. Any strictly necessary cookies are limited to
        making the site work. [Confirm and list any cookies actually set before launch.]
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy; the "last updated" date above will always reflect the current version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
